<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoOperationAdd</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to implement addition</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Operation.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoValue *SilikoOperationAdd(int argc, SilikoValue **argv);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoOperationAdd</function> function calculates
the sum of the values passed in <varname>argv</varname> where
<varname>argc</varname> is the number of values passed.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoOperationAdd</function> returns a pointer to an
object representing the result of the addition operation.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Conformance</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoOperationAdd</function> function conforms to
Siliko Core’s interface for pure functions and can be installed into a
<type>SilikoEngine</type> if wrapped with
<function>SilikoPureFunctionCreate</function>.</para>
</refsection>
